 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Split some splitting wood into smaller chunks so they take less time to burn. A pile of kindling on top helps too. They do, surprisingly. Sprinkle them around the base and they soak up moisture from the air. About three times the diameter of the bowl. Then you only need fire about the size of a ten bowl, with a proper air gap so it doesn't overheat and burn your lip. Make sure it' out of reach of bedding and clothes, and away from any windows. A small rock on top keeps it burning all night.",
